  "id": "psychodynamic-diagnostic-manual",
  "term": "Psychodynamic Diagnostic Manual",
  "definition": "The Psychodynamic Diagnostic Manual is a psychodynamic framework for understanding and assessing mental functioning, including a person’s use of unconscious defenses. Its second edition also includes an Infancy and Early Childhood section that can be used to describe the quality of the mother–infant relationship, although it was not created as a parenting manual.",
